   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Finance Corporation</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HDB Debt Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IFC anticipates that the proposed investment will increase access to finance for the underserved micro, small, and medium enterprises (MSMEs) particularly self-employed borrowers/microentrepreneurs and women borrowers, thereby enabling them to expand their businesses, generate income, support families, and contribute to their economic empowerment. 
Beyond the project level outcomes, IFC anticipates that this investment will promote greater competitiveness via demonstration and replication channels, by showcasing the potential and viability of scaling up low-ticket financing to underserved self-employed borrowers and women borrowers.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project comprises of senior debt investment for up to US$200 million in HDB Financial Services Limited (HDB or the Company) for a tenor of up to 5 years, in one or more tranches. The Company will utilize IFCs investment proceeds for growing its loan book towards micro and small enterprises (MSEs) and self-employed borrowers/microentrepreneurs, including women borrowers. A part of IFCs investment proceeds will also be utilized by the Company for financing purchase of electric vehicles (EVs) and energy-efficient consumer goods (EECGs).</narrative>
  </description>
